It is really important to have magic resistance and reflection, so if
you are stuck with the gray scale mail + shield of reflection combo (as
opposed to silver scale mail + cloak of magic resistance combo), then
you can't use a 2-handed weapon like Mjollnir.  Werebane might be the
best choice, since it will do extra silver damage against some
monsters.  A crysknife would do slightly more damage to non-silver
hating monsters.  You can create a crysknife by enchanting a wormtooth,
and you can find a wormtooth when you kill a worm.  You might want to
carry both of these, and switch weapons depending on what you are
fighting.

I don't think anything protects fire destroyable items from fire traps.
 You can gain fire resistance to prevent damage to you, and fireproof
burnable equipment to protect them from getting burnt, but I think you
need to place fire destroyable items in sacks to keep them safe from
fire traps.

The best way to deal with a disenchanter is probably to gather a stack
of daggers from the Gnomish Mines, and throw the daggers at the
disenchanter.  If the disenchanter gets too close, engrave Elbereth
with a wand of digging, and resume the dagger throwing once the
disenchanter moves away.



